            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Latin for an extra family name, then the Latin for a guardian."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: adulēscentia, adulēscentiae",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "adulēscentia, adulēscentiae — \"young adulthood, youth\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In adulēscentiā multa et stulta fēcī. In my youth I did many foolish things."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine, from adulēscēns (taught): roughly from fifteen to thirty. English adolescence."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "adulēscentia is built on adulēscēns, the participle of adulēscō, \"to grow up\" (Lewis & Short). English adolescence comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
