              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pūpillus, pūpillī — \"a ward, an orphan boy\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Tūtor pecūniam pūpillī fidēliter servābat. The guardian faithfully kept the ward's money safe."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine. The girl is a pūpilla, also 'the pupil of the eye'. English pupil."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pūpillus is a diminutive of pūpulus, \"little child\" (Lewis & Short): a little child in the care of another. English pupil comes from it through French."
            }
          ]
        },
